repository-code: 'https://github.com/OpenKNX/OFM-DFA.git'
url: 'https://github.com/OpenKNX/OFM-DFA'
abstract: >-
  OFM-DFA is an OpenKNX module that enables universal modeling of state-dependent
  behavior for KNX building automation systems based on Deterministic Finite Automata
  (DFA) with optional extensions. The module allows users to configure state machines
  directly via the KNX ETS (Engineering Tool Software), with multiple channels each
  representing an automaton definition supporting up to 16 different states. State
  transitions are triggered by up to 8 different inputs or state-specific timeouts,
  with 4 configurable outputs supporting various common data point types (DPTs).
  The module is designed for event-oriented processing of state-dependent behavior
  that depends on the sequence or temporal progression of events in KNX installations.
  Configuration is performed using a two-dimensional state transition table in ETS,
  making complex automation logic accessible without custom programming. The module
  integrates with other OpenKNX modules, particularly the Logic Module (OFM-LogicModule),
  for preprocessing input values and enabling sophisticated building automation scenarios.
  Optional extensions include conditional state transitions based on logic channel outputs,
  reconstruction after restart, execution interruption and direct state invocation.
date-released: 2025
